{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.UniversalIlpAlgorithm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.UniversalIlpAlgorithm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.universal_ilp_selects_minimum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.universal_ilp_selects_minimum","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L102-L114","doc":"**The LP selects the minimum-crossing feasible knot operator**, as a\npredicate: `K` is feasible (`universal_ilp q state K`) and no feasible\noperator has strictly fewer crossings. This names the LP's optimality\ncondition (§3b). The previous\n`(hmin : K.cr ≤ K'.cr) : K.cr ≤ K'.cr := hmin` self-assumingly\nre-projected the given comparison and asserted nothing about the LP. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.universal_ilp_holds_of_zero_gram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.universal_ilp_holds_of_zero_gram","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L85-L100","doc":"**The LP currently constrains nothing, and this proves it.**  With the\nzero placeholder for `gram_matrix`, `universal_ilp` holds of *every*\nknot operator, at every `q` and every `state`.\n\nReported rather than hidden (AGENTS.md \"report honest negatives\"): the\nvacuity was already stated in `gram_matrix`'s docstring, where nothing\nchecked it.  A machine-checked statement goes stale the moment a real\nGram lands — this theorem will simply stop compiling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.universal_ilp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.universal_ilp","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L72-L83","doc":"The universal ILP: min cr(K) s.t. K ∈ knots \\ {1}, G · NF(x · K) ≥ 0.\n\nTwo conjuncts were dropped as redundant, not as a weakening:\n`K.is_knot` and `K.crossing_number > 0` are now **guaranteed by the\nstructure** (`is_knot`, `is_nontrivial`), so restating them here added\nnothing.  Before this change the first was worse than redundant — it\nwas the free universe-`Prop` field, satisfiable by `True`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.frobenius_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.frobenius_positive","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L68-L70","doc":"Frobenius positivity: G · x ≥ 0 componentwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.gram_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.gram_matrix","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L44-L66","doc":"The Frobenius Gram matrix G of H₃(q) — **a zero placeholder**, and the\nLP built on it therefore constrains nothing\n(`universal_ilp_holds_of_zero_gram` below proves this, rather than\nleaving it as a docstring claim).\n\n**Docstring corrected 2026-09-14.** This said the intended `G(q)`\n(Halverson–Ram seminormal Gram on the 6-dimensional `H₃(q)`) \"is\nsharper\".  Under the canonical convention D (`z = q³/(q²+1)`, owner\nruling 2026-08-15) that understates it: the real Gram is **singular**.\n`mass-theory/frobenius-gram-matrix` records that `y_(1³) = 0`\nsymbolically, so the `(1³)` Wedderburn block *is* the radical of the\nform, `det G = 0` **exactly** (not numerically — at rational `q` the\nwhole Gram is rational under D), and `G⁻¹` does not exist; `pyhecke`\nexports `G_PINV` on the quotient `H₃(q)/rad` instead, with `RADICAL`\nthe q-antisymmetriser `Σ_w (−1/q)^ℓ(w) T_w`.\n\nSo wiring the real Gram is not a drop-in: `frobenius_positive` over a\nrank-5 form is a different condition, and picking how the radical\ndirection is treated is a modelling choice, not a transcription.  Left\nto the author; NOT changed here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.knotOperator_isEmpty_of_never_single_component","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.knotOperator_isEmpty_of_never_single_component","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L36-L42","doc":"The structure is refutable: no knot operator exists over a predicate\nthat holds of nothing.  The previous `is_knot : Prop` admitted\n`is_knot := True` and so could not be empty for any `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.is_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.is_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.is_knot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.is_knot","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L33-L33","doc":"The closure is a single component — a **proof**, discharged by the\ncaller against their own `IsSingleComponent`, not a proposition the\nconstructor picks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.crossing_number","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.crossing_number","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.coeffs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.coeffs","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L26-L26","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Interactions.KnotOperator","kind":"structure","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/universal-ilp-algorithm.lean#L15-L34","doc":"A knot operator in H₃(q) represented by its NF coefficients.\n\n`IsSingleComponent` is **caller-supplied**: the predicate that decides\nwhether a coefficient vector with a given crossing number closes to a\nsingle-component braid.  It is a parameter rather than a field because a\nfield typed with the *universe* `Prop` holds a proposition as data — the\nconstructor then chooses it, `True` is a legal choice, and the `is_knot`\nconjunct in `universal_ilp` below was satisfied for free.\n\nParameterising makes the structure **refutable**: see\n`knotOperator_isEmpty_of_never_single_component`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}